-- חוק דמי מחלה (היעדרות עקב הריון ולידה של בת זוג), התש"ס-2000 — sections
-- 1, 3 and 4: up to seven days a year an employee may charge to his accrued
-- sick leave for his partner's pregnancy treatments or tests or her giving
-- birth, by the rules the Minister set; that the law adds to every other
-- right; and that the State is an employer like any other. The text is
-- laws/sick-pay-partner-pregnancy-law.toml, pinned from the live page of
-- ספר החוקים הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: the takanon's §1.25.3.1 restates §1 as its clause 6,
-- with the Minister's rules on which absences qualify, and cites the law.
-- §2's rules are the Minister's regulations, not pinned.

IMPORT prelude

§ `חוק דמי מחלה (היעדרות עקב הריון ולידה של בת זוג) — שבעה ימים בשנה`

§§ `1`

-- Up to seven days a year of absence, by the Minister's rules, for
-- treatments or tests connected with his partner's pregnancy, or for her
-- giving birth, charged to his accrued sick leave.
@ref law:1
`days a year section 1 of the Partner Pregnancy Law gives` MEANS 7

#ASSERT `days a year section 1 of the Partner Pregnancy Law gives` EQUALS 7

§§ `3`

-- The law adds to an employee's right by law or agreement and takes none
-- away: for a right measured in one number, the larger stands.
@ref law:3
GIVEN `what the law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what the instrument gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what stands under section 3 of the Partner Pregnancy Law` `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives` IS
    max `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives`

#ASSERT `what stands under section 3 of the Partner Pregnancy Law` 7 7 EQUALS 7

§§ `4`

-- For this law the State as employer is like any other employer.
@ref law:4
`the Partner Pregnancy Law binds the State as an employer` MEANS TRUE
